  "description": "Elongated solitons in GS History+Wave Niches: four species that grow into still worms and rods, from the corner of feed and kill where one species alone grows long. F 0.062 k 0.0567 (top left: a long curly worm), 0.066 0.058 (top right: long straight rods), 0.07 0.057 (bottom left: rods) and 0.07 0.06 (bottom right: short worms and spots; same tint as bottom left, sharing its feed). Together their shared history spreads wider than any one alone and pulls feed down into spot territory, so each feels it at half strength (history1..4 = 0.5); each starts as a large patch of noise. All four still there at 120k steps in two runs out of two. The balance is touchy: the curly worm took over at k 0.0565 and once died at 0.0568. View c (the history) tinted by P_F; b1…b4 to see one species alone.",
